Subject: [PATCH 2/6] geph5-misc-rpc: point the control socket at /data/adb on Android

Android has no writable /run, so the unix default of /run/geph/control.sock
cannot be created. The root/KernelSU-managed module owns a persistent directory
at /data/adb/geph5, which is also where platform.rs's state_dir() puts the
state. Keeping the socket in the same subtree as the state it describes means
one directory to back up and one to clean on uninstall.

Upstream touching this file does not make the patch fragile: it is a pair of
cfg-gated constants, and Android is handled by adding a third arm rather than
by editing the existing ones.

---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libraries/geph5-misc-rpc/src/manager_control.rs b/libraries/geph5-misc-rpc/src/manager_control.rs
index 62f5916..b466654 100644
--- a/libraries/geph5-misc-rpc/src/manager_control.rs
+++ b/libraries/geph5-misc-rpc/src/manager_control.rs
@@ -17,8 +17,12 @@ use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
 #[cfg(target_os = "macos")]
 pub const MANAGER_CONTROL_SOCK: &str = "/var/run/geph/control.sock";
 /// Filesystem path of the manager's control socket.
-#[cfg(all(unix, not(target_os = "macos")))]
+#[cfg(all(unix, not(any(target_os = "macos", target_os = "android"))))]
 pub const MANAGER_CONTROL_SOCK: &str = "/run/geph/control.sock";
+/// Android has no writable /run; use the persistent /data/adb area that the
+/// root/KernelSU-managed module owns.
+#[cfg(target_os = "android")]
+pub const MANAGER_CONTROL_SOCK: &str = "/data/adb/geph5/control.sock";
 /// Name of the manager's control named pipe.
 #[cfg(windows)]
 pub const MANAGER_CONTROL_PIPE: &str = r"\\.\pipe\geph-manager-control";
